{%- if include_web %}
Docker Hub publishing
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The release workflow always publishes the Docker image to GHCR
(``ghcr.io/{{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}}``) using the built-in
``GITHUB_TOKEN`` — no setup needed. To *additionally* publish to Docker Hub:

**[HUMAN]** Create an
`access token <https://app.docker.com/settings/personal-access-tokens>`_ with
**Read & Write** scope.

**[AGENT]** Set **both** repository secrets:

.. code-block:: sh

   gh secret set DOCKERHUB_USERNAME --repo {{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}}
   gh secret set DOCKERHUB_TOKEN --repo {{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}}

**[CHECK]**

.. code-block:: sh

   gh secret list --repo {{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}} --json name \
     --jq '(["DOCKERHUB_USERNAME","DOCKERHUB_TOKEN"] - [.[].name]) == []' | grep -qx true

The pair is all-or-nothing: with neither set, the workflow skips Docker Hub with
a notice and publishes to GHCR only; with only one set, a preflight job fails
fast and blocks every publish channel (PyPI included) so a misconfiguration can
never produce a partial release. The image is pushed to
``docker.io/<DOCKERHUB_USERNAME>/{{github_repo_name}}``, so the namespace
follows the Docker Hub account — it does not need to match the GitHub owner.
{%- endif %}
