Homebrew tap
~~~~~~~~~~~~

The release workflow does not build a {% if primary_executable %}cask{% else %}formula{% endif %} itself — it sends a
``repository_dispatch`` event to your ``{{github_user}}/homebrew-tap`` repo,
whose own listener workflow bumps the {% if primary_executable %}cask{% else %}formula{% endif %} and opens a PR there. Full
one-time setup (creating the tap, bootstrapping the initial {% if primary_executable %}cask{% else %}formula{% endif %}, and
installing the listener) is documented in
:doc:`../packaging/homebrew-tap/README`.

.. toctree::
   :hidden:

   ../packaging/homebrew-tap/README

The only piece owned by **this** repo is the dispatch credential:

**[HUMAN]** Create a fine-grained PAT with **Contents: write** on
``{{github_user}}/homebrew-tap`` (no ``Pull requests`` scope needed — the tap
opens its own PR with its own ``GITHUB_TOKEN``).

**[AGENT]** Set it as the ``HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN`` repository secret:

.. code-block:: sh

   gh secret set HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN --repo {{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}}

**[CHECK]**

.. code-block:: sh

   gh secret list --repo {{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}} --json name \
     --jq 'any(.[]; .name == "HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN")' | grep -qx true

When unset, the ``bump-homebrew`` job skips with a notice (never fails the
release).
{%- endif %}
