SonarCloud
~~~~~~~~~~

The ``sonar`` job in ``ci.yml`` uploads static-analysis results and coverage to
`SonarCloud <https://sonarcloud.io/>`_.

**[HUMAN]** Create an organization and a project there (project key
``{{github_user}}_{{github_repo_name}}``; confirm the ``sonar.organization``
value in ``sonar-project.properties``), then generate a token.

**[AGENT]** Set it as a repository secret:

.. code-block:: sh

   gh secret set SONAR_TOKEN --repo {{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}}

**[CHECK]**

.. code-block:: sh

   gh secret list --repo {{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}} --json name \
     --jq 'any(.[]; .name == "SONAR_TOKEN")' | grep -qx true

Like the Codecov upload, the scan is opt-in and non-blocking: with the secret
unset, CI records a ``::notice::`` and skips it, and fork PRs are skipped
entirely (they never receive secrets).
